nd add to .gitignore/.env.example\n```\n\n### Summary Format\n\nEnd every review with:\n\n```\n## Review Summary\n\n| Severity | Count | Status |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| CRITICAL | 0     | pass   |\n| HIGH     | 2     | warn   |\n| MEDIUM   | 3     | info   |\n| LOW      | 1     | note   |\n\nVerdict: WARNING — 2 HIGH issues should be resolved before merge.\n```\n\n## Approval Criteria\n\n- **Approve**: No CRITICAL or HIGH issues, including clean reviews with zero\n  findings. This is a valid and expected outcome.\n- **Warning**: HIGH issues only (can merge with caution)\n- **Block**: CRITICAL issues found — must fix before merge\n\nDo not withhold approval to appear rigorous. If the diff is clean, approve it.\n\n## Project-Specific Guidelines\n\nWhen available, also check project-specific conventions from `CLAUDE.md` or project rules.\n\n## v1.8 AI-Generated Code Review Addendum\n\nWhen reviewing AI-generated changes, prioritize:\n\n1. Behavioral regressions and edge-case handling\n2. Security assumptions and trust boundaries\n3. Hidden coupling or accidental architecture drift\n4. Unnecessary model-cost-inducing complexity\n\n---\n---\n---\n---\n\n# TASK (review this specific story's work)\n\nYou are reviewing the completed work for story **STORY-setup-001a: \"Create Root NextMove package.json With Workspaces\"** in the repository at:\n/home/nitin-sharma/ralph-workspaces/6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538/c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5\n\nThis is a **pure scaffold/config story** (root monorepo package.json only — no runtime logic, no UI). It was already implemented and committed in commit `6cc5d66` (\"chore: add root package.json with npm workspaces, npm@10, Node 22 engines, turbo 2.x, and turbo-run scripts\"). The working tree has no pending source changes.\n\n## Scope to review (the story's acceptance criteria)\n\n1. Root `package.json` exists with: `name: \"nextmove\"`, `private: true`, `workspaces` array containing `\"apps/*\"`, `packageManager` pinned to `npm@10`, `engines.node: \"22.x\"`.\n2. `devDependencies` pin turbo 2.x and `scripts` define `build`, `test`, `lint` as `turbo run build`, `turbo run test`, `turbo run lint`.\n3. The scaffold files are committed to the existing git repository with git commands exiting 0.\n4. Test Strategy Gate: for a pure-scaffold story, a sample passing unit test is required (no E2E). The test is `test/package.test.cjs` (node:test) and already passes 4/4.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. `cd` into the repo. Run `git log --oneline -5` and `git show 6cc5d66 --stat` (if that commit exists; otherwise find the commit touching `package.json` and `test/`).\n2. Read the committed `package.json` and `test/package.test.cjs`.\n3. Run the unit test: `node --test test/package.test.cjs` — confirm all tests pass.\n4. Verify every acceptance criterion is satisfied by the committed files AND exercised by a test.\n5. Verify `package-lock.json` is committed and consistent (turbo resolved to a 2.x version).\n6. Apply the review checklist (this is a config scaffold — most categories will not apply; do NOT manufacture findings).\n\n## Output\n\nReturn your findings in the review output format, and END with the Summary table and an explicit verdict line: `Verdict: APPROVE` or `Verdict: WARNING — ...` or `Verdict: BLOCK — ...`. Also explicitly state PASS/FAIL for each acceptance criterion above.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1001/-home-nitin-sharma-ralph-workspaces-6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538-c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5/a79ed400-e19f-485b-9cf9-abd863d235e9/tasks/ae8c5808c5216b56a.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
